{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"Ticket 6 (byzantine-spinelike-penguin, FINAL ticket) implemented: pass3_decide stops stamping severity at all 5 return sites; shim.py passes through explicit severity unchanged, omits when absent (deleted _KERNEL_TO_COMMON_SEVERITY/_SEVERITY_DEFAULT); normalize_finding only clamps present-but-invalid values, never backfills absent ones; common.schema.json relaxes severity to optional; removed vestigial BLOCKING_SEVERITIES/SEVERITIES/_severities_env from review_bot/config.py + updated its 2 tests; fixed a docs-drift gate (gen_env_registry.py/env-vars.md) the implementer caught; wrote release-notes.md/CHANGELOG.md compatibility notes and amended ADR 0108 myself. TDD held-out loop: implementer got per-layer happy-path tests (5 files), held out the full-chain integration test (shim->finalize_findings->normalize_finding->final review_result has no severity key -- the exact composition defect the gate caught) which validated GREEN after implementation, confirming the layers compose correctly. Mutation-teeth check in sandbox on the critical normalize_finding guard (mutated to always-clamp, confirmed the absent-key test goes RED while the present-invalid test stays green -- proving both behaviors independently tested). Full suite: 18318 passed, same 13 pre-existing environmental failures as before, zero regressions. Hit and resolved a real rebase conflict in generated docs/env-vars.md (4 sibling tickets landed to origin/main ahead of this one -- resolved by regenerating via the script, not hand-merging). Pushed to Gerrit: https://rebar.solutions.navateam.com/c/rebar/+/2462."},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1788156997072921685,"uuid":"338a552d-c0b3-4a30-9f19-50c73629b096"}